  "senses": [
    {
      "n": 1,
      "signpost": null,
      "definition": "added to an adjective to make a noun that names the quality or state the adjective describes",
      "explanation": "**-ness** attaches to a great many adjectives, especially everyday ones, and to forms in **-ed** or **-ing** (*tiredness*, *willingness*); the noun is usually uncountable. Adjectives from Latin often prefer **-ity** (*curious*, *curiosity*; *able*, *ability*), and some adjectives have their own noun (*strong*, *strength*; *wise*, *wisdom*; *hot*, *heat*), so check before making a **-ness** word. A final **y** becomes **i**: *happy*, *happiness*.",
      "grammar": {
        "countability": "uncountable",
        "transitivity": null,
        "codes": [],
        "patterns": []
      },
      "labels": {
